(r"""| PROSPERITY → the PAY | ST's ONE funding read for a settlement holder: `fundingBandOf`'s settlement arm — `prosperityRank01 < 0.2` `unfunded` · `< 0.45` `meagre` · `< 0.8` `funded` · else `lavish` (ST §2.4) — the treasury's paid share when W-COIN lights (RULINGS-ROUND2 D: new `UPKEEP_LEDGERS` rows when W-COIN lights; a `patrols` row beside `sites` and `retainers` — the W-COIN inbox); the DM's `wages` overlay wins |""",
r"""| PROSPERITY → the PAY | THE BAND, always on: the settlement's PROSPERITY-DERIVED band from the landed ladder, through ST's ONE band law exported SETTLEMENT-keyed (`fundingBandOfSettlement(worldState, settlementId, snapshot)`, ST's settlement arm — `prosperityRank01 < 0.2` `unfunded` · `< 0.45` `meagre` · `< 0.8` `funded` · else `lavish`, ST §2.4; the export is a route row to ST's disposition); the DM's `wages` overlay is a CEILING over it — EFFECTIVE = min(the DM's band, the purse's band) (RULINGS-ROUND2b ST-r2-1: one band law for sites and riders), so a town whose prosperity falls lets its riders thin before W-COIN lights. THE COIN is separate and a slot: when W-COIN lights, the treasury's `UPKEEP_LEDGERS` gain a `patrols` row beside `sites` and `retainers` (RULINGS-ROUND2 D; the W-COIN inbox; its leaf-first car named there) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — SEAMS-r2-12: the owner's eighth word ("gated by … prosperity") stays live whatever the coin's state; ST's read was SITE-keyed] |"""),
