(r"""- **PEACE** — the town's courts at peace and nothing believed near: `fielded = ceil(max × PEACE_SHARE)`, `PEACE_SHARE` 0.6 ("less during peacetime").
- **A BELIEVED THREAT** in the territory or on a stretch of the round (§5.1) — `fielded` rises toward `max` by the threat's believed band (one step per band above `thin`, DRAFT).
- **AT WAR** — the town in a live war front, or an enemy army believed in its land: `fielded = max` for the first-response weeks (§9.1).
- **THE LEVY MARCHES** — the town's army deployed abroad (`deployments[id].targetId`): by default the riders are ABSORBED into it (`fielded = 0` beyond the minimum one rider at the seat; a `losses`-free absorption, written as nothing — the riders are with the army); a court whose chooser KEEPS its riders (§9.1(e)) holds `fielded` at its peace share and pays `patrolDraw` (PR3).
- **THE TOWN BESIEGED** — the riders are inside the walls: `fielded = 0` on the roads; they are part of `homeDefense` already.
- **THE DM'S ORDER** may lift `fielded` to `max` or hold it at the minimum (§11.1); never beyond the envelope.""",
r"""- **PEACE** — the town's courts at peace and nothing believed near: `fielded = ceil(max × peaceShare)`, `peaceShare = clamp(PEACE_SHARE + PEACE_POSTURE_W × (0.5 − appetite01) + PEACE_ALIGN_W × harsh01, 0.4, 1.0)` — `PEACE_SHARE` 0.6 ("less during peacetime"), the court's own risk appetite (`strategicPosture.js :: courtRiskAppetiteOf`: a wary court keeps more riders out, a bold or lax one fewer; `PEACE_POSTURE_W` 0.4) and the seat's alignment (`settlementAlignment`: a lawful-cruel seat leans to the watch, `harsh01` = lawfulness × malice; `PEACE_ALIGN_W` 0.2) — all DRAFT, UNMEASURED; where the posture layer is dark, the flat 0.6. This fork is what keeps every rider out in quiet years, and it is what §7.5's harassment prices [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-27: no court fork existed, so the counterforce punished only the DM's own order].
- **A BELIEVED THREAT** in the territory or on a half of the round (§5.1) — `fielded` rises toward `max` by the threat's believed band (one step per band above `thin`, DRAFT).
- **AT WAR AT HOME** — the town in a live war front with its army at home, or an enemy army believed in its land: `fielded = max` for the first-response weeks (§9.1).
- **THE ARMY ON CAMPAIGN** (the town's army deployed abroad, `deployments[id].targetId`) — MORE than in peace, as the owner's first word asks ("more during wartime … if they have an army in a campaign"): the riders the court keeps are set ONCE, when the army is raised — by default `kept = ceil(max × CAMPAIGN_SHARE)`, `CAMPAIGN_SHARE` 0.75 (DRAFT, UNMEASURED; above the peace share), and up to `max` where the court's chooser keeps more (`keepRiders`, §9.1(e)); the kept riders are drawn from the army's seed at that deploy (`patrolDraw`, PR3, stamped on the deployment record, §2.7), and while that army is out `fielded` never exceeds them. They ride THE ARMY'S ROAD FIRST — the halves of its path out through the town's own land, its supply road (§2.2's first priority term) — then the rest of the round in priority order; whatever halves they do not reach go UNPATROLLED, and the back roads go to the brigands (felt sentence 9). Everything not kept marched with the army (ABSORBED — written as nothing; the riders are with the army) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-3 (BLOCKING): as compiled, an army on campaign held `fielded` at or below the PEACE share even when the court kept its riders, so "more during wartime" could never hold for the case the owner named · PR-r2-1: the draw at deploy].
- **THE TOWN BESIEGED** — the riders are inside the walls: `fielded = 0` on the roads; they are part of `homeDefense` already.
- **THE DM'S ORDER** may lift `fielded` to `max` or hold it at the minimum (§11.1); never beyond the envelope, and while an army is out never beyond what it left at home."""),
(r"""5. **The round** — the remaining riders are placed on their stretches by the cadence hash (§2.3).""",
r"""5. **The round and the placement** — the remaining riders are placed on their halves by the round's order and the periodic clock (§2.3); the stage writes the coming week's `placement` (`next` for t+1; the old `next` moved to `lived`; the coverage ring advanced) — the ONE placement every consumer of t+1 reads (PR4) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-15]."""),
(r"""**Clock** (requirement 9): weekly; the stage runs AFTER the danger step (`advanceEmbattlement`, kernel ~2391) and before the next tick's consumers, so the presence subtraction a week's coverage earns is felt on the roads the following tick (read-last, write-next — the same order ST states for sites).""",
r"""**Clock** (requirement 9): weekly. The stage runs at `advanceCalamity`'s head (kernel l.2527) — AFTER every consumer of the week: `ageRoamingStressors` (l.510, the counter term's stamp), `advanceSettlementSupply` (l.843, banditry and smuggling), `advanceRumorLedgers` (l.2097, reports), `advanceEnvoyDiplomacyPulse` (l.2194, THE ONE PERSON STAGE's encounters), `advanceEmbattlement` (l.2391, the slow half), `advanceArmyTransit` (l.2442, the witness and the screen). So the placement it writes at tick t for t+1 is exactly the placement every consumer reads in t+1 — read-last, write-next made STRUCTURAL by the stored digest, never by re-derivation; a pin asserts that every consumer of one week names the same placement (R30). [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-15: nothing was stored, so "read-last/write-next" had no write to read and consumers re-derived from different mid-tick states (ordering CONFIRMED, `cure/D-PR-r2.md` §1(f)).]"""),
(r"""A weekly placement is exactly the host document's own model (presence per stretch per week, by hash), it costs one hash per stretch-week, and it gives the DM the only fact that matters: which roads were watched this week.""",
r"""A weekly placement is exactly the host document's own model (presence per stretch per week, by address — a phase fixed by hash), it costs one stored row per town per week, and it gives the DM the only fact that matters: which roads were watched this week."""),
